verdicts.summary:
The atmos lane fails round 3 with a lens score of 7.8: one major and one nit; the other 11 checks pass. All files are in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-muhamadrifaldi-Documents-GitHub-retrux-hero-rnd/a0f5735b-9a7f-477e-9b57-6de40ca5644b/scratchpad/work2/atmos/judge3/; the verdict is verdict_draft.md there.

The user's main complaint is fixed in this lane. The clouds stay on screen however long the page idles, and the loop wraps never show. Tested with 400 s of real-time idle, clock jumps out to 7 days, and every pointer view. MAIN still has the old clouds that disappear, and this verdict holds the lane back from merging.

**What still fails (major):** when the mist builds, the lower half of the mountain looks like grey smog. The reference shows darker blue slopes under white fog, and they get bluer as the mist thickens. At reference frame S320 the lower massif's blue-minus-red value is 49.3 in the reference and 31.2 in the lane; in real time it never gets above 35. The bank at the mountain's base also lacks the reference's billows and moves about half as much. Two things in Atmos.ts cause it:
- the card light darkens each pixel in its own colour instead of shifting it toward blue;
- the fog layer (HAZE_VEIL) is one flat grey-blue colour instead of white patches over blue slopes.

The fix is narrow (fog colour and the card light's tint) and does not touch the cloud fix.

**Nit:** with the pointer to the left, one fogged ice slab in the foreground shows as a flat pale rectangle with hard edges.

**Correction to my earlier draft:** I withdrew the minor "dark ridge face 8 levels too light". It came from comparing boxes without shifting the reference by its true offset (+8, +4 px). Aligned, the lane is within +1.5 to +2.9 of the reference, closer than round 10. Only the ridge's colour gap remains, as part of the major.

**What passes:**
- the cards no longer make the mountain glow;
- no pops under pointer sweeps;
- press, hold and release;
- the `?atmos=r10` switch back to round 10;
- all 21 switches;
- other quality tiers and screen sizes, including phone;
- typecheck;
- a test merge onto MAIN, with no errors and the rings unchanged.

Frame-time cost is +8.2 to +8.5 % at rest, +5.3 to +5.7 % in the mist, and +1.6 to +8.0 % in the hold, inside the 10 % budget. The Mac was on battery with the user active, so I compared ratios only. The water lane's cost will add to this once both are merged.

**Merge note:** Water.ts carries a 5-line hook from this lane, so it has to be re-applied if the water lane's Water.ts is merged later.

I stopped my lab on :5176 and killed the one perf process that hung after printing its numbers. :5173 is up, but the Next dev server on :3000 was already down when I resumed at 22:09 and needs restarting; that is MAIN's server, so I left it. I appended a judge-round-3 section to LANE/HANDOFF.md and the steps to WORK/LOG.md; no lane code was changed.
